      "common:shortName": [],
      "common:generalComment": [
        {
          "#text": "Commodity plastics or commodity polymers are plastics produced in high volumes for applications where exceptional material properties are not needed. They are used in packaging, food containers, and household products. Unlike engineering plastics, commodity plastics are inexpensive to produce and exhibit relatively weak mechanical properties. The most popular types include polyethylene, polypropylene, polystyrene, polyvinyl chloride, and polyethylene terephthalate.",
          "@xml:lang": "en"
        },
        {
          "#text": "商品塑料或商品聚合物是大量生产的塑料，用于不需要特殊材料属性的应用。它们被用于包装，食品容器和家庭产品。与工程塑料不同，商品塑料生产成本低，且机械性能相对较弱。最受欢迎的类型包括聚乙烯，聚丙烯，聚苯乙烯，聚氯乙烯和聚对苯二甲酸乙二醇酯。",
          "@xml:lang": "zh"
        }
      ],
